WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.139
Villains, villains, and more villains.

00:00:03.139 --> 00:00:07.750
Every year, New York Comic Con offers interesting
glimpses into the not-so-distant future of

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:08.750
entertainment.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.480
This year, "Star Trek" fans have more than
a little to be happy about, thanks to a new

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.299
teaser trailer for the upcoming "Star Trek:
Picard" Season 3.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:19.710
The brand new New York Comic Con teaser for
the new "Picard" season revolves around a

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:25.369
shocking distress call Admiral Jean-Luc Picard
receives from Beverly Crusher, and an extra-threatening

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:27.070
villain known as Vadic.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.010
However, that's just the beginning of Picard's
troubles this time around.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:35.390
Even by "Star Trek: Picard" standards, there
are some extremely intriguing character reveals

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.860
here, and they have fans all saying the same
thing.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.600
Professor James Moriarty makes his grand entrance
in the teaser saying "Greetings, old friends,"

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.719
armed with a smirk, an icy-cold stare, and
a gun.

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:49.570
The hologram Sherlock Holmes villain from
"Star Trek: The Next Generation" isn't the

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.570
only bad guy from the show to reemerge in
the Season 3 teaser, either.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:57.360
Just when you thought everything was over,
Lore stares down the heroes with an extremely

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.360
unamused look on his face.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.930
Fans have reacted to the news of the villains'
return with a combination of surprise and

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.420
delighted intrigue.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:05.779
One redditor wrote about Moriarty,

00:01:05.779 --> 00:01:10.020
"That was a TNG villain I would have never
guessed about coming back at this point."

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.289
Another agreed, saying,

00:01:11.289 --> 00:01:15.179
"Moriarty is my favorite character from Star
Trek so you can only imagine my reaction when

00:01:15.179 --> 00:01:16.179
he appeared.

00:01:16.179 --> 00:01:17.880
I would have never expected that."

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.999
Lore drew similar comments from fans.

00:01:19.999 --> 00:01:21.270
A Reddit commenter wrote,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:25.130
"I called 'where is Lore' before the first
season came out...didn't think it would actually

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.130
pan out."

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.849
Other corners of the internet also took note
of the villain reveals.

00:01:28.849 --> 00:01:30.399
A YouTube commenter wrote,

00:01:30.399 --> 00:01:31.399
"Holy s—.

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:32.579
Moriarty and Lore.

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:35.969
Hopefully this will be the send off the TNG
crew so rightly deserves."

00:01:35.969 --> 00:01:40.919
Meanwhile, over on Twitter, one user couldn't
hide their exclamation mark-heavy excitement,

00:01:40.919 --> 00:01:41.919
writing,

00:01:41.919 --> 00:01:42.919
"O.M.G!!!!!!

00:01:42.919 --> 00:01:46.069
Just watched the trailer for Picard season
3 ! Moriarty &amp; Lore are back!!!!!!!

00:01:46.069 --> 00:01:47.679
I can hardly wait!"

00:01:47.679 --> 00:01:51.649
Both returning villains have deep ties to
"Star Trek: The Next Generation" protagonists.

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:55.799
The "Star Trek" version of James Moriarty
is actually a highly ambitious hologram that

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:00.289
was originally created by Geordi La Forge,
but soon becomes a self-aware bad guy.

00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:04.950
Meanwhile, Lore is Data's fellow Soong-type
android who's ... well, significantly less

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.990
friendly than his more famous compatriot.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:11.629
While neither Moriarty nor Lore are one-and-done
villain of the week types, they both have

00:02:11.629 --> 00:02:16.250
but a small handful of episodes under their
belts — two for Moriarty, and four for Lore.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.879
As such, they're both known enemies that longtime
fans can get excited about, yet easily deep

00:02:20.879 --> 00:02:25.010
enough cuts to offer all sorts of fascinating
options for "Picard" Season 3.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:29.129
Judging by their ominous stares in the trailer,
everyone who gets in their way is definitely

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:31.069
in for a deliciously bad time.

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:35.109
The return of these old villains continues
"Picard's" all but stated mission to revisit

00:02:35.109 --> 00:02:39.579
the vast majority of "The Next Generation"
characters, minor and major alike — and

00:02:39.579 --> 00:02:43.959
in Lore's case, Spiner's continued tendency
to constantly portray new characters in the

00:02:43.959 --> 00:02:44.959
show.

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:48.930
How the evil android and the hologram Napoleon
of Crime fit in the grand scheme of things

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:53.120
remains to be seen, but fans can already rest
assured that "Picard" Season 3 will feature

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.159
a pretty neat rogues gallery.

